 "mechanism": {
  "statement": "A fresh cheap search stops at exactly min(maxVisits, cheapSearchVisits) = 100 visits and a fresh full search at exactly 600 (cpp/search/search.cpp:509,579-580 count the reused root visits numNonPlayoutVisits toward maxVisits). Selfplay always clears the tree before a full search (cpp/program/play.cpp:1567 asserts clearBotBeforeSearch for forSelfPlay; :1234 clears) but NOT before a cheap search when cheapSearchTargetWeight <= 0 (play.cpp:1147 sets clearBotBeforeSearchThisMove = false). A cheap search that inherits a subtree already holding >= 100 visits therefore does zero new playouts and logs the inherited count, a value strictly between 100 and 600. The probe's discriminator 'Root visits > cheapSearchVisits' (codes/eval/probe_search_9x9.py, CHEAP_SEARCH_VISITS) bins every such cheap search as full.",
  "prediction_tested": "a value strictly between 100 and 600 can only follow a 600 or another between value in the same game, never a 100, and never opens a game",
  "result": "holds exactly on the probe run (0 of 667 follow a 100; 533 follow a 600; 134 follow a between; 0 open a game) and on the loop's 80 random-net games (0 of 543 follow a 100; 449 follow a 600; 93 a between; 1 opens a game, in that run's reduceVisits=true/fork regime, which also has 48 values outside [100, 600])"
 },
 "verdict": "The 0.34171 recorded in probe_search_nofork-299259.json is reproduced to the last digit by the '> 100' rule and is an instrument artefact: 667 of the 2529 turns it binned as full are cheap searches on a reused subtree. Counting only Root visits == maxVisits gives 1862/7401 = 0.25159 on this run and 2311/9211 = 0.25090 on the loop's 80 random-net games. The attempt-1 and attempt-2 20-game rows cannot be re-binned (their logs, sgfs and npz were deleted by the probe script's rm -rf) but ran the same instrument."
}